To implement Variable Length Quantity (VLQ) encoding and decoding, I will update
`lib.rs` with the logic for `to_bytes` and `from_bytes`.



1.  **`to_bytes`**: For each `u32` value, we extract 7 bits at a time from the 
least significant bits. We continue until the value is 0. For all bytes except 
the last one, we set the most significant bit (bit 7) to 1 to indicate that more
bytes follow. The last byte has bit 7 set to 0.

2.  **`from_bytes`**: We iterate through the input bytes. We accumulate the 7 
significant bits of each byte into a `u32` result. If the most significant bit 
of the current byte is 0, it means this is the last byte of the current number, 
so we push the accumulated result to the output vector and reset the 
accumulator. If the most significant bit is 1, we continue to the next byte. If 
we run out of bytes while expecting more (i.e., the last byte processed had bit 
7 set), we return an `IncompleteNumber` error.



